 up and 2 steps left.\n\nSo 5s move 2 steps toward the block? But (3,8) \u2192 (3,5) is 3 steps left, not 2.\n\nHmm, (3,5) is adjacent to block at col 4. From col 8 to col 5 is 3 steps.\n\nLet me try: 5s move until they're adjacent to the block (Chebyshev distance 1 or Manhattan distance 1).\n\nFrom (0,3): need to reach row \u22652 (to be adjacent to rows 3-4). So move to row 2. That's (2,3).\nFrom (3,8): need to reach col \u22645 (to be adjacent to cols 3-4). So move to col 5. That's (3,5).\nFrom (7,7): need row \u22645, col \u22645. Move to (5,5).\n\nYes! 5s move to be adjacent to the 2x2 block (Chebyshev distance 1), moving the minimum distance needed.\n\n```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    import copy\n    result = copy.deepcopy(grid)\n    \n    # Find the 2x2 block of 2s\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0]) if rows > 0 else 0\n    \n    block_top, block_left = -1, -1\n    for r in range(rows - 1):\n        for c in range(cols - 1):\n            if grid[r][c] == 2 and grid[r][c+1] == 2 and grid[r+1][c] == 2 and grid[r+1][c+1] == 2:\n                block_top, block_left = r, c\n                break\n        if block_top != -1:\n            break\n    \n    if block_top == -1:\n        return result  # No block found\n    \n    block_bottom, block_right = block_top + 1, block_left + 1\n    \n    # Collect 5 positions\n    fives = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 5:\n                fives.append((r, c))\n                result[r][c] = 0  # Clear original 5\n    \n    # Move each 5 to be adjacent to the block\n    for r5, c5 in fives:\n        # Find closest position adjacent to block (Chebyshev distance 1 from any block cell)\n        # Block spans [block_top, block_bottom] x [block_left, block_right]\n        # Target: rows in [block_top-1, block_bottom+1], cols in [block_left-1, block_right+1]\n        # but not inside the block itself\n        \n        # Clamp to be adjacent\n        if r5 < block_top:\n            nr = block_top - 1\n        elif r5 > block_bottom:\n            nr = block_bottom + 1\n        else:\n            nr = r5  # Same row as block, keep row but move col\n        \n        if c5 < block_left:\n            nc = block_left - 1\n        elif c5 > block_right:\n            nc = block_right + 1\n        else:\n            nc = c5  # Same col as block, keep col but move row\n        \n        # If we'd be inside the block, adjust\n        if block_top <= nr <= block_bottom and block_left <= nc <= block_right:\n            # Need to move outside - push to nearest edge\n            # This happens when 5 is inside the block's row/col range\n            # Pick the direction to move\n            if r5 <= block_top:\n                nr = block_top - 1\n            else:\n                nr = block_bottom + 1\n            if c5 <= block_left:\n                nc = block_left - 1\n            else:\n                nc = block_right + 1\n        \n        # Ensure in bounds\n        nr = max(0, min(rows - 1, nr))\n        nc = max(0, min(cols - 1, nc))\n        \n        result[nr][nc] = 5\n    \n    return result\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    import copy\n    result = copy.deepcopy(grid)\n    \n    # Find the 2x2 block of 2s\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0]) if rows > 0 else 0\n    \n    block_top, block_left = -1, -1\n    for r in range(rows - 1):\n        for c in range(cols - 1):\n            if grid[r][c] == 2 and grid[r][c+1] == 2 and grid[r+1][c] == 2 and grid[r+1][c+1] == 2:\n                block_top, block_left = r, c\n                break\n        if block_top != -1:\n            break\n    \n    if block_top == -1:\n        return result  # No block found\n    \n    block_bottom, block_right = block_top + 1, block_left + 1\n    \n    # Collect 5 positions\n    fives = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 5:\n                fives.append((r, c))\n                result[r][c] = 0  # Clear original 5\n    \n    # Move each 5 to be adjacent to the block\n    for r5, c5 in fives:\n        # Find closest position adjacent to block (Chebyshev distance 1 from any block cell)\n        # Block spans [block_top, block_bottom] x [block_left, block_right]\n        # Target: rows in [block_top-1, block_bottom+1], cols in [block_left-1, block_right+1]\n        # but not inside the block itself\n        \n        # Clamp to be adjacent\n        if r5 < block_top:\n            nr = block_top - 1\n        elif r5 > block_bottom:\n            nr = block_bottom + 1\n        else:\n            nr = r5  # Same row as block, keep row but move col\n        \n        if c5 < block_left:\n            nc = block_left - 1\n        elif c5 > block_right:\n            nc = block_right + 1\n        else:\n            nc = c5  # Same col as block, keep col but move row\n        \n        # If we'd be inside the block, adjust\n        if block_top <= nr <= block_bottom and block_left <= nc <= block_right:\n            # Need to move outside - push to nearest edge\n            # This happens when 5 is inside the block's row/col range\n            # Pick the direction to move\n            if r5 <= block_top:\n                nr = block_top - 1\n            else:\n                nr = block_bottom + 1\n            if c5 <= block_left:\n                nc = block_left - 1\n            else:\n                nc = block_right + 1\n        \n        # Ensure in bounds\n        nr = max(0, min(rows - 1, nr))\n        nc = max(0, min(cols - 1, nc))\n        \n        result[nr][nc] = 5\n    \n    return result",
